\section{Algorithms and numerical comparison}

\textbf{Exact channel values.} Enumerate $G$ as permutations, bucket by the dial, apply \eqref{eq:count} in each bucket, and average. This costs $O(|G|\,n)$. \textbf{Bayes error.} In each bucket, subtract the largest type tally from the bucket size, and sum. \textbf{Prime types.} For $p\ge5$ let $d=\gcd(p-1,6)$. Then $T(p)=d$ if $2^{(p-1)/d}\equiv1\pmod p$, and $T(p)=0$ otherwise. This costs $O(\log p)$ multiplications.

